  'privacy.title': "Privacy",
  /** HTML */
  'privacy.body': "<p>You can use Niflaot <b>without an account</b>: then your progress is kept only in your browser (localStorage) and sent nowhere.</p><h3>Who is responsible</h3><p>The Torah project MyChitas, <a href=\"mailto:Office@mychitas.app\">Office@mychitas.app</a>.</p><h3>What we keep if you create an account</h3><ul><li>your email — to sign in with a code;</li><li>your nickname, age group (14+ or under 14), language;</li><li>for children under 14 — a parent's email and the record of their consent;</li><li>your progress in the lessons and in the Gematria of the Day, points and streak;</li><li>the classes you are in or teach;</li><li>the number of questions to the AI teacher per day (not their text).</li></ul><h3>Why and on what basis</h3><p>To keep your progress on all your devices, to show classes, and to count the questions to the AI teacher. The basis is your consent (Art. 6 (1) a GDPR), for children under 14 — a parent's consent (Art. 8 GDPR, § 4 DSG). You can withdraw consent at any time by deleting the account.</p><h3>Who sees what</h3><p>Your nickname and points — the teacher of a class you join; they are not shown to other players. Nobody but us sees your email.</p><h3>“Quiz together”</h3><p>No account is needed to play. The name you enter in a room and your answers are kept on the server (Cloudflare) only while the room is open (no longer than 6 hours), are seen by the host and the players of that room, and are then erased with it. They are not added to an account or to your progress. You don’t have to use your real name.</p><h3>Where it is kept and who helps</h3><ul><li>Cloudflare — the server for accounts, the AI teacher and reminders;</li><li>Resend — sends the sign-in codes and the emails to parents;</li><li>Anthropic — answers the questions to the AI teacher (questions are sent there but not stored by us);</li><li>GitHub Pages — the site itself; GoatCounter — visit statistics without cookies;</li><li>Google, Apple, Mozilla — deliver notifications if you turned them on.</li></ul><h3>Microphone</h3><p>The microphone turns on only if you tap “Sing into the microphone” in the karaoke of a niggun. Your voice is analyzed in the browser, on your device (its pitch — in tune or not); nothing is saved or sent to the site. Your singing is recorded only if you tick “Record my singing”: the recording stays in the browser’s memory while the page is open — to listen to, download or send from your phone’s share menu (to whom is up to you); it never goes to the site or our server. The microphone turns off when the singing ends or you leave the page.</p><h3>How long</h3><p>As long as the account exists. A child's account without a parent's consent is deleted after 30 days, an unfinished sign-up after 7 days.</p><h3>Your rights</h3><p>You can ask what data we keep about you, correct it or delete it — the “Delete account” button on the account page deletes everything at once. Questions — to <a href=\"mailto:Office@mychitas.app\">Office@mychitas.app</a>. You can also complain to the Austrian Data Protection Authority (Datenschutzbehörde, dsb.gv.at).</p>",
